---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Getting Started — QualiLens" description="Download QualiLens from GitHub, install the requirements, and run your first analysis in minutes.">

  <!-- Header -->
  <section class="bg-gradient-to-b from-brand-50 to-white pt-20 pb-16">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6">
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold mb-4">Getting Started</h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-text-secondary leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">QualiLens runs entirely on your computer. Download it from GitHub, install three things, and your first analysis is minutes away.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Step 1: Requirements -->
  <section class="py-16 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-6">
        <span class="shrink-0 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-brand-600 text-white text-sm font-bold flex items-center justify-center">1</span>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Check the requirements</h2>
      </div>

      <p class="text-text-secondary mb-6">QualiLens builds its own environment on first launch. Three things must already be on your computer.</p>

      <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-6">
        <table class="w-full text-sm border border-border rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
          <thead class="bg-surface">
            <tr>
              <th class="text-left py-3 px-4 font-medium text-text-muted">Requirement</th>
              <th class="text-left py-3 px-4 font-medium text-text-muted">Why</th>
              <th class="text-left py-3 px-4 font-medium text-text-muted">Check</th>
              <th class="text-left py-3 px-4 font-medium text-text-muted">Install</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="text-text-secondary">
            <tr class="border-t border-border">
              <td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium text-text-primary">Python 3.11+</td>
              <td class="py-3 px-4">Runs the backend and analysis pipelines</td>
              <td class="py-3 px-4"><code class="text-xs bg-surface px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">python3 --version</code></td>
              <td class="py-3 px-4"><code class="text-xs bg-surface px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">brew install python@3.12</code> or <a href="https://python.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-brand-500 hover:underline">python.org</a></td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-t border-border">
              <td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium text-text-primary">Node 18+ &amp; npm <span class="text-text-muted font-normal">(clone only)</span></td>
              <td class="py-3 px-4">Builds the interface once, on first launch. Not needed if you downloaded the release ZIP</td>
              <td class="py-3 px-4"><code class="text-xs bg-surface px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">node -v</code></td>
              <td class="py-3 px-4"><a href="https://nodejs.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-brand-500 hover:underline">nodejs.org</a></td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-t border-border">
              <td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium text-text-primary">ffmpeg <span class="text-text-muted font-normal">(optional)</span></td>
              <td class="py-3 px-4">Extracts audio from video; splits large recordings</td>
              <td class="py-3 px-4"><code class="text-xs bg-surface px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">ffmpeg -version</code></td>
              <td class="py-3 px-4"><code class="text-xs bg-surface px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">brew install ffmpeg</code></td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <p class="text-sm text-text-muted">You can skip ffmpeg if you only upload documents and audio files under about 24 MB. You will need it for video or large audio files.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="border-border max-w-4xl mx-auto" />

  <!-- Step 2: Download -->
  <section class="py-16 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-6">
        <span class="shrink-0 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-brand-600 text-white text-sm font-bold flex items-center justify-center">2</span>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Download QualiLens</h2>
      </div>

      <p class="text-text-secondary mb-6">Download the latest release, unzip it, and place the folder wherever you like. The release includes the pre-built interface — you need only Python, no Node or npm.</p>

      <a href="https://github.com/iconerr/qualilens/releases/latest/download/QualiLens.zip" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2.5 px-5 py-3 rounded-xl bg-brand-600 text-white font-semibold hover:bg-brand-500 transition-colors mb-4">
        <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M4 16v2a2 2 0 002 2h12a2 2 0 002-2v-2M7 10l5 5 5-5M12 15V3" /></svg>
        Download QualiLens.zip
      </a>

      <p class="text-sm text-text-muted mb-4">Developers who want to modify the code can clone the repository instead — this path requires Node 18+ to build the interface on first launch.</p>

      <div class="bg-text-primary rounded-xl p-5 mb-4 overflow-x-auto">
        <code class="text-sm text-green-400 font-mono">git clone https://github.com/iconerr/qualilens.git</code>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-amber-50 border border-amber-200 rounded-xl p-4 flex gap-3">
        <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-amber-500 shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 9v3.75m-9.303 3.376c-.866 1.5.217 3.374 1.948 3.374h14.71c1.73 0 2.813-1.874 1.948-3.374L13.949 3.378c-.866-1.5-3.032-1.5-3.898 0L2.697 16.126zM12 15.75h.007v.008H12v-.008z"/></svg>
        <p class="text-sm text-amber-800"><strong>Cloud sync warning.</strong> If the folder sits inside a Dropbox, iCloud, or OneDrive directory, never run QualiLens on two computers against the same synced database simultaneously. Let the sync finish completely before opening the app on a second machine.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="border-border max-w-4xl mx-auto" />

  <!-- Step 3: Launch -->
  <section class="py-16 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-6">
        <span class="shrink-0 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-brand-600 text-white text-sm font-bold flex items-center justify-center">3</span>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Launch QualiLens</h2>
      </div>

      <p class="text-text-secondary mb-4">Open a terminal in the QualiLens folder and run the launcher.</p>

      <div class="bg-text-primary rounded-xl p-5 mb-4 overflow-x-auto">
        <code class="text-sm text-green-400 font-mono">./run.sh</code>
      </div>

      <p class="text-text-secondary mb-4">The first run creates a Python environment, installs dependencies, and builds the interface — expect a minute or two. Every launch after the first is much faster. Once the server is up, it prints the address and opens your browser.</p>

      <div class="bg-text-primary rounded-xl p-5 mb-6 overflow-x-auto">
        <code class="text-sm text-gray-400 font-mono">QualiLens running at http://127.0.0.1:8765  (Ctrl-C to stop)</code>
      </div>

      <p class="text-sm text-text-muted">Stop the app with <kbd class="px-1.5 py-0.5 bg-surface text-text-primary rounded text-xs font-mono border border-border">Ctrl-C</kbd> in the terminal. Closing the browser tab does not stop it — runs continue in the background.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="border-border max-w-4xl mx-auto" />

  <!-- Step 4: API keys -->
  <section class="py-16 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-6">
        <span class="shrink-0 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-brand-600 text-white text-sm font-bold flex items-center justify-center">4</span>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Add an API key</h2>
      </div>

      <p class="text-text-secondary mb-4">Open <strong>Settings</strong> from the top bar. Each provider gets its own card with Save, Test, and Remove controls. Paste your key, press Save, then Test to confirm it works.</p>

      <p class="text-text-secondary mb-4">You need a key from at least one of the four providers: Anthropic, OpenAI, Google, or Mistral. If you plan to upload audio or video, you also need an OpenAI key — transcription always runs through OpenAI's Whisper service regardless of which provider performs the analysis.</p>

      <div class="bg-surface rounded-xl border border-border p-5">
        <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary"><strong>Where keys are stored.</strong> Keys live in the local SQLite database as plain text — not encrypted, not in a system keychain. Use <strong>Remove</strong> before sharing the folder or handing the computer to someone. Prefer a key scoped to this work, with its own spending limit.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="border-border max-w-4xl mx-auto" />

  <!-- Step 5: First analysis -->
  <section class="py-16 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-6">
        <span class="shrink-0 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-brand-600 text-white text-sm font-bold flex items-center justify-center">5</span>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Run your first analysis</h2>
      </div>

      <p class="text-text-secondary mb-4">Click <strong>New analysis</strong> and the five-step wizard walks you through everything: choose a method, configure it, select a model, upload your data, and review the cost estimate before starting.</p>

      <p class="text-text-secondary mb-4">Start with one short document. A first run costs cents, not dollars, and it lets you see every checkpoint before you commit a real dataset.</p>

      <div class="bg-surface rounded-xl border border-border p-5">
        <h3 class="font-semibold mb-3">Accepted file types</h3>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 text-xs font-mono">
          <span class="px-2.5 py-1 bg-white rounded-lg border border-border">.txt</span>
          <span class="px-2.5 py-1 bg-white rounded-lg border border-border">.md</span>
          <span class="px-2.5 py-1 bg-white rounded-lg border border-border">.docx</span>
          <span class="px-2.5 py-1 bg-white rounded-lg border border-border">.pdf</span>
          <span class="px-2.5 py-1 bg-white rounded-lg border border-border">.rtf</span>
          <span class="px-2.5 py-1 bg-white rounded-lg border border-border">.mp3</span>
          <span class="px-2.5 py-1 bg-white rounded-lg border border-border">.mp4</span>
          <span class="px-2.5 py-1 bg-white rounded-lg border border-border">.m4a</span>
          <span class="px-2.5 py-1 bg-white rounded-lg border border-border">.wav</span>
          <span class="px-2.5 py-1 bg-white rounded-lg border border-border">.webm</span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs text-text-muted mt-3">Audio and video require an OpenAI key for transcription. Video also requires ffmpeg.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Updating -->
  <section class="py-16 bg-surface">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Updating QualiLens</h2>
      <p class="text-text-secondary mb-4">Open <strong>Settings</strong> and find the Application card. <strong>Check for updates</strong> asks GitHub for the latest release — one request, nothing of yours sent with it. When a newer release exists, <strong>Download and install</strong> fetches and applies it through a validated updater that replaces only application files and never touches your projects, keys, or uploads.</p>
      <p class="text-text-secondary">After the update the app stops itself. Start it again with <code class="text-xs bg-white px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded font-mono border border-border">./run.sh</code>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Citation -->
  <section class="py-12 bg-white border-t border-border">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3">Citing QualiLens</h2>
      <p class="text-text-secondary text-sm mb-4">Please cite QualiLens if it contributes to published research. Name the version, the provider, and the model in your methods section — those determine your analysis far more than the application does.</p>
      <div class="bg-surface rounded-xl border border-border p-4 font-mono text-sm text-text-secondary">
        Aggarwal, A., &amp; Commuri, S. (2026). <em>QualiLens: A local application for LLM-assisted qualitative data analysis</em> [Computer software].
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
